X-WR-TIMEZONE:America/New_York
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pittsburg2026-000@stephen
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260805T220000Z
DTEND:20260805T221000Z
SUMMARY:Cut the plywood pier plate
DESCRIPTION:Set the tripod up FIRST at the exact leg extension you'll use
  and measure the triangle before drilling. Forstner recesses ~1/2in wide
 \, 1/4in deep. Mark which corner faces north. Tape-mark the leg extensio
 n.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT0M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Cut the plywood pier plate
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pittsburg2026-001@stephen
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260805T223000Z
DTEND:20260805T224000Z
SUMMARY:Set mount latitude to 45 deg
DESCRIPTION:EQ6-R altitude bolt from 42.8 to 45.1. Do it in the driveway\
 , not in the dark. Same for the SAM's latitude wedge.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT0M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Set mount latitude to 45 deg
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pittsburg2026-002@stephen
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260808T160000Z
DTEND:20260808T161000Z
SUMMARY:Rental lens should be here
DESCRIPTION:Confirm Canon EF mount. Decentering test: star field\, compar
 e all four corners at 100%. Then aperture sweep at 35mm: f/1.8\, 2.0\, 2
 .2\, 2.5.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT0M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Rental lens should be here
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pittsburg2026-003@stephen
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260810T150000Z
DTEND:20260810T151000Z
SUMMARY:Verify 12V regulation under load
DESCRIPTION:WARNING: 4S pack reaches 16.8V\, EQ6-R is rated 11-16V. Meter
  the distribution box under load and confirm 12.0-13.8V out.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT0M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Verify 12V regulation under load
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pittsburg2026-004@stephen
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260809T160000Z
DTEND:20260809T161000Z
SUMMARY:Subscribe to ntfy on phone
DESCRIPTION:Topic name is in remote-astro/FIELD_OPS.md. Star-lost\, merid
 ian-flip\, low-disk alerts reach you over cell from the lake.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT0M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Subscribe to ntfy on phone
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pittsburg2026-005@stephen
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260810T220000Z
DTEND:20260810T221000Z
SUMMARY:Pack
DESCRIPTION:Desktop + monitors + cables. Extension cord. 50ft ethernet. P
 lywood plate. Pavers. Bubble level. Spare SD cards. Two headlamps (one r
 ed\, one warm-white). Amber gel. 72mm UV/IR filter. Multimeter. IR therm
 ometer gun. ID.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT0M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Pack
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pittsburg2026-006@stephen
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260811T190000Z
DTEND:20260811T191000Z
SUMMARY:ARRIVE - unload the truck
DESCRIPTION:Move fast. Every minute before dark is load-bearing today.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT30M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:ARRIVE - unload the truck
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pittsburg2026-007@stephen
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260811T192000Z
DTEND:20260811T193000Z
SUMMARY:360 HORIZON SURVEY - do this first
DESCRIPTION:Phone app\, mark the treeline from the exact spot the tripod 
 will stand. Dense every 5 deg across 170-240. That band is where M8/M20\
 , the core and the Trifid all live.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT5M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:360 HORIZON SURVEY - do this first
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pittsburg2026-008@stephen
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260811T194500Z
DTEND:20260811T195500Z
SUMMARY:Pick positions
DESCRIPTION:EQ6 spot (clear north for Polaris - watch for eaves and the n
 orth wall\, not trees). 6SE spot far enough that walking to it doesn't s
 hake the rig. Canon spot. Desktop. Find the AC outlet and measure the ru
 n.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT5M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Pick positions
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pittsburg2026-009@stephen
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260811T200000Z
DTEND:20260811T201000Z
SUMMARY:Desktop setup indoors\, then run the ethernet
DESCRIPTION:Tower\, monitors\, power. Run the 50ft ethernet out to where 
 the Pi will sit. Do this after picking the mount spot\, not before.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT5M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Desktop setup indoors\, then run the ethernet
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pittsburg2026-010@stephen
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260811T204500Z
DTEND:20260811T205500Z
SUMMARY:Plate down\, tripod on it\, level to the bubble
DESCRIPTION:Pavers underneath if the ground is soft - seat them roughly c
 oplanar or the plywood rocks. Note the leg extension against your tape m
 arks.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT5M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Plate down\, tripod on it\, level to the bubble
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pittsburg2026-011@stephen
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260811T211500Z
DTEND:20260811T212500Z
SUMMARY:Head on\, counterweights\, OTA\, balance
DESCRIPTION:Balance RA on the counterweight shaft and DEC in the dovetail
 .
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT5M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Head on\, counterweights\, OTA\, balance
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pittsburg2026-012@stephen
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260811T220000Z
DTEND:20260811T221000Z
SUMMARY:Cabling and power - USB FIRST
DESCRIPTION:All USB connected before the Pi gets power. Hot-plug crashes 
 the Pi 5. Boot\, wait for the beep\, Ekos connects\, verify all five dev
 ices.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT5M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Cabling and power - USB FIRST
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pittsburg2026-013@stephen
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260811T223000Z
DTEND:20260811T224000Z
SUMMARY:Site coords in - virtualgps on the Pi
DESCRIPTION:ssh astro / sudo nano /etc/systemd/system/virtualgps.service 
 / set 45.088279\, -71.324767 + elevation / sudo systemctl daemon-reload 
 / sudo systemctl restart virtualgps / cat /tmp/vgps to confirm. Then che
 ck the site in Ekos. Wrong coords means wrong LST and wrong meridian-fli
 p timing. Cool to -10C. Daylight focus\, EAF step 500.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT5M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Site coords in - virtualgps on the Pi
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pittsburg2026-014@stephen
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260811T230000Z
DTEND:20260811T231000Z
SUMMARY:Daylight flats
DESCRIPTION:~0.005s at gain 100 with the panel. These cover all three nig
 hts unless you rotate the camera or change the optical train.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT5M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Daylight flats
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pittsburg2026-015@stephen
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260812T003000Z
DTEND:20260812T004000Z
SUMMARY:Set park position = home/Polaris
DESCRIPTION:Verify ON_COORD_SET=TRACK\, never SYNC.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT5M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Set park position = home/Polaris
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pittsburg2026-016@stephen
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260812T004500Z
DTEND:20260812T005500Z
SUMMARY:POLAR ALIGN
DESCRIPTION:Polaris is up. Take your time - tonight's alignment is the on
 e you reproduce for the rest of the trip.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT5M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:POLAR ALIGN
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pittsburg2026-017@stephen
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260812T011000Z
DTEND:20260812T012000Z
SUMMARY:*** MARK THE PLATE ***
DESCRIPTION:Stake it\, outline it\, both. Mark which corner faces north. 
 Then DO NOT TOUCH THE ALT/AZ BOLTS again all trip. This is what makes ni
 ghts 2 and 3 possible.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT5M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:*** MARK THE PLATE ***
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pittsburg2026-018@stephen
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260812T011500Z
DTEND:20260812T012500Z
SUMMARY:Plate-solve test\, autofocus V-curve\, start guiding
DESCRIPTION:Step 30\, 15 steps. Target HFR ~1.2.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT5M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Plate-solve test\, autofocus V-curve\, start guiding
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pittsburg2026-019@stephen
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260812T015600Z
DTEND:20260812T020600Z
SUMMARY:ASTRONOMICAL DARK - scope to M8/M20
DESCRIPTION:120s subs\, gain 100\, offset 50\, dither 3px. THE ONLY NIGHT
  the refractor can reach this pair - on lake nights it's below 10 deg be
 fore you get back.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT10M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:ASTRONOMICAL DARK - scope to M8/M20
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pittsburg2026-020@stephen
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260812T020000Z
DTEND:20260812T021000Z
SUMMARY:6SE - the southern showpieces
DESCRIPTION:M8\, M17 Swan\, M16 Eagle\, M22\, M11\, M20. Invisible from h
 ome and only up now. This is the why-did-we-drive-here moment.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT5M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:6SE - the southern showpieces
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pittsburg2026-021@stephen
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260813T041500Z
DTEND:20260813T042500Z
SUMMARY:Scope to the Veil / Cygnus Loop
DESCRIPTION:Just past its 12:17 transit so it's west of the meridian - no
  flip all night. Teal OIII and crimson Ha filaments.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT10M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Scope to the Veil / Cygnus Loop
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pittsburg2026-022@stephen
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260813T043000Z
DTEND:20260813T044000Z
SUMMARY:Canon to the meteor field
DESCRIPTION:20s\, f/1.8\, ISO 3200\, continuous.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT5M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Canon to the meteor field
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pittsburg2026-023@stephen
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260813T060000Z
DTEND:20260813T061000Z
SUMMARY:Perseids building
DESCRIPTION:6SE on NGC 7331 + Stephan's Quintet while it's high. Then M31
 \, M33\, Saturn.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT15M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Perseids building
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pittsburg2026-024@stephen
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260813T074500Z
DTEND:20260813T075500Z
SUMMARY:Twilight - stop capture
DESCRIPTION:Then TEARDOWN PRACTICE: pull the OTA and counterweights\, lif
 t the head off without touching alt/az\, and move it TO THE PORCH - that
 's where it lives for the rest of the trip. Time yourself\, you repeat t
 his twice.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT15M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Twilight - stop capture
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pittsburg2026-025@stephen
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260812T210000Z
DTEND:20260812T211000Z
SUMMARY:Assemble the rig ON THE PORCH
DESCRIPTION:Head\, counterweights\, OTA\, balance RA and DEC\, cables dre
 ssed. Comfortable and lit - this is where the why-wont-it-connect half-h
 ours normally happen.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT15M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Assemble the rig ON THE PORCH
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pittsburg2026-026@stephen
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260812T214500Z
DTEND:20260812T215500Z
SUMMARY:Pi up\, Ekos connected - START COOLING
DESCRIPTION:All five devices verified. Porch is at ambient so -10C is an 
 easy 22C delta. DEW HEATERS OFF - under a roof it cannot dew\, and heat 
 fights the acclimation. The triplet needs these five hours to reach ambi
 ent.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT5M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Pi up\, Ekos connected - START COOLING
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pittsburg2026-027@stephen
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260812T221500Z
DTEND:20260812T222500Z
SUMMARY:Check the tripod outside
DESCRIPTION:Still seated on the plate\, bagged\, level. Alt/az bolts unto
 uched so alignment carries over.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT5M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Check the tripod outside
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pittsburg2026-028@stephen
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260812T230000Z
DTEND:20260812T231000Z
SUMMARY:LOAD THE CAR - lake kit
DESCRIPTION:6SE + fork + tripod + eyepieces + 32mm Plossl (LEAVE THE EQ W
 EDGE HOME). Canon + Sigma with the 72mm UV/IR filter fitted + lens hood.
  SAM + tripod\, wedge at 45. POWER\, one supply per system: LP-E17 batte
 ries for the camera (all four\, charged) - USB power bank for the dew st
 rap - lead-acid + FUSED alligator lead for the 6SE - 2xAA lithiums plus 
 spares for the SAM. Power box and coupler stay in the truck as backup. U
 SB dew strap. Power bank + hand warmers as backup. Spare SD cards. IR th
 ermometer. Two headlamps + amber gel. Something to drop the tripod to 0.
 5m. Chairs\, layers\, bug spray\, ID.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT20M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:LOAD THE CAR - lake kit
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pittsburg2026-029@stephen
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260812T231500Z
DTEND:20260812T232500Z
SUMMARY:DEPART - moose drive north on Route 3
DESCRIPTION:The 6SE's best targets are southern and only up 9:56 to midni
 ght - exactly when you're at the lake. Leave it behind and M8\, M17\, M1
 6\, M22 and M11 do not happen this trip. Sunset 7:58.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT10M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:DEPART - moose drive north on Route 3
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pittsburg2026-030@stephen
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260813T001000Z
DTEND:20260813T002000Z
SUMMARY:Earth's shadow + Belt of Venus
DESCRIPTION:Azimuth 112\, off your right heading north. Dark band with a 
 pink edge rising out of the east. Gone by 8:35. ~1/10s\, f/5.6\, ISO 100
 \, underexpose slightly.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT5M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Earth's shadow + Belt of Venus
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pittsburg2026-031@stephen
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260813T003000Z
DTEND:20260813T004000Z
SUMMARY:Arrive the lake - set up
DESCRIPTION:Civil twilight ends. Tripod and SAM out immediately.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT5M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Arrive the lake - set up
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pittsburg2026-032@stephen
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260813T004500Z
DTEND:20260813T005500Z
SUMMARY:FOREGROUND FRAMES - only chance
DESCRIPTION:Glow still on the water. f/2.8\, ISO 800\, 60-120s. These are
  your blend layer and there is no second chance tonight.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT5M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:FOREGROUND FRAMES - only chance
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pittsburg2026-033@stephen
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260813T010000Z
DTEND:20260813T011000Z
SUMMARY:Polar align the SAM - frame to azimuth 204
DESCRIPTION:Polaris is behind you over land. SAM latitude wedge should be
  at 45.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT5M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Polar align the SAM - frame to azimuth 204
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pittsburg2026-034@stephen
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260813T011500Z
DTEND:20260813T012500Z
SUMMARY:Focus\, check corners\, lock composition
DESCRIPTION:Hard deadline isn't darkness\, it's being ready for it.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT5M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Focus\, check corners\, lock composition
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pittsburg2026-035@stephen
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260813T015600Z
DTEND:20260813T020600Z
SUMMARY:ASTRONOMICAL DARK - shoot the core
DESCRIPTION:Landscape\, 18mm. Also several at 35mm: Rho Oph + core + Trif
 id in one frame. Rho Oph is at 13.2 deg and dying - shoot it FIRST.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT10M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:ASTRONOMICAL DARK - shoot the core
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pittsburg2026-036@stephen
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260813T023000Z
DTEND:20260813T024000Z
SUMMARY:RHO OPH DEADLINE - below 10 deg\, gone for the year
DESCRIPTION:Last frames of Rho Oph now. Core at 13.6 and sliding toward f
 rame centre.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT15M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:RHO OPH DEADLINE - below 10 deg\, gone for the year
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pittsburg2026-037@stephen
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260813T030000Z
DTEND:20260813T031000Z
SUMMARY:Switch to PORTRAIT
DESCRIPTION:Band standing vertical out of the water. Core dead centre at 
 11.8 deg. This is the postcard.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT5M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Switch to PORTRAIT
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pittsburg2026-038@stephen
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260813T032500Z
DTEND:20260813T033500Z
SUMMARY:CORE DEADLINE - 10 deg. South is finished
DESCRIPTION:Last frames. Pack up.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT15M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:CORE DEADLINE - 10 deg. South is finished
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pittsburg2026-039@stephen
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260813T034500Z
DTEND:20260813T035500Z
SUMMARY:Depart the lake
DESCRIPTION:Moose peep on the way back to the cabin.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT5M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Depart the lake
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pittsburg2026-040@stephen
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260813T041000Z
DTEND:20260813T042000Z
SUMMARY:Back at the cabin
DESCRIPTION:Check ntfy / dashboard. Pull the SD card\, copy to the deskto
 p\, verify two or three frames opened and are sharp. Fresh card in.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT0M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Back at the cabin
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pittsburg2026-041@stephen
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260813T041500Z
DTEND:20260813T042500Z
SUMMARY:Carry the scope out from the porch
DESCRIPTION:Already at ambient\, camera already cold. Onto the tripod - a
 lt/az untouched\, so this Polar align CHECK - the plate may have shifted
  and the ground settles\, so expect a small adjustment. Not from scratch
 . DEW HEATERS ON NOW\, low setting. Target 2-5C above ambient\, no more 
 - err low on the triplet.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT5M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Carry the scope out from the porch
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pittsburg2026-042@stephen
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260813T050000Z
DTEND:20260813T051000Z
SUMMARY:Scope on Cocoon IC 5146 + B168
DESCRIPTION:Red core\, blue rim\, black dust river - the best colour targ
 et of the trip. Transits 1:19 at 87.8 deg\, essentially zenith. WARNING:
  near-zenith meridian flips are the awkward ones. Supervise it\, or star
 t after 1:25 and skip the flip entirely.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT10M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Scope on Cocoon IC 5146 + B168
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pittsburg2026-043@stephen
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260813T050000Z
DTEND:20260813T051000Z
SUMMARY:Canon meteor run - Cassiopeia/M31 field
DESCRIPTION:20s\, f/1.8\, ISO 3200\, continuous. Radiant in the lower-lef
 t corner. Dew heater on the lens.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT5M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Canon meteor run - Cassiopeia/M31 field
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pittsburg2026-044@stephen
DTSTAMP:20260802T000000Z
DTSTART:20260813T060000Z
DTEND:20260813T061000Z
SUMMARY:PERSEID PEAK HOURS
DESCRIPTION:Radiant climbs 47 to 61 deg. Rates roughly triple over the ev
 ening. Camera runs itself - both of you outside\, in chairs\, looking up
 .
